                <pb facs="0740" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg678"/>

                <p rendition="#center">(Deposited at Monterey May 1, 1878. Received at the city of
                    Mexico at 12.45 p.m.)</p>
                <p>Department of Gubernation, under date of the 29th.</p>
                <p>General Can ales sends me the following:</p>
                <p>“Lieut. Col. Encarnacion Garza has routed 100 men at Capote of those enlisted in
                    Texas. Among them were Americans and colored men from the State of Texas.”</p>
                <closer><signed>C. GARZA GARCIA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
